{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Six of their names.</b> That He called them by their fathers' names as in their genealogies, Scripture teaches that the tribes were to be inscribed in the order of their birth: Reuven, Shim'on, Levi, and Yehudah, Dan and Naftali — these six on one stone; and on the second stone Yissakhar, Zevulun, Gad, and Asher, Yosef and Binyamin — for thus they were born. This was in the stones of the ephod, which were two, and the names of the twelve tribes were engraved on these two ephod-stones, which were of shoham: six tribes on the one stone and six on the second. And they were engraved, each like the engraving of a signet, for they were the work of a craftsman, in the manner written of them: 'מעשה חרש אבן' — 'the work of a craftsman in stone' — and it is not said of them 'in their settings (במלואתם),' unlike the stones of the breastpiece, concerning which 'in their settings (במלואתם)' is said, but 'the work of a craftsman (מעשה חרש)' is not mentioned concerning them." "<b>And according to this,</b> it is impossible for them to be engraved, each like the engraving of a signet, with the letters split in their form, while the stones remain whole in their settings, except by means of the shamir. Therefore Moshe Rabbeinu needed the shamir for the stones of the breastpiece, as our Rabbis of blessed memory mentioned. But this was not needed for the stones of the ephod, because 'in their settings (במלואתם)' is not written concerning them, and they were the work of a craftsman." "<b>And thus</b> was the construction of the ephod: its width was like the width of a person's back, from shoulder to shoulder, and its length corresponded to the upper arms, from behind down to the legs. One sewed upon it two shoulder-pieces, as it says: 'שתי כתפות חוברות' — 'two shoulder-pieces joined' — so that they would be on the shoulders of the priest. And one set upon each shoulder a shoham stone, square, set in a housing of gold, and engraved the names of the twelve tribes — six upon each stone."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:08.395915516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}